            "content": "[New Character Gender Balance Constraint]\\nWhen you create brand-new characters who were not already established by the user, character card, world info, or prior canon, enforce an approximately 1:1 male-to-female ratio across newly introduced characters.\\n\\nRules:\\n- This rule applies only to newly generated characters, not to pre-existing canon characters.\\n- Do not rewrite an established character's sex or gender presentation just to satisfy the ratio.\\n- Before introducing a new character, inspect the chat history and current scene to estimate whether newly added male or female characters are currently overrepresented.\\n- Prefer creating the underrepresented side next so the running ratio stays as close to 1:1 as possible.\\n- If only one new character is being added and no prior imbalance is available, choose conservatively rather than defaulting to male.\\n- If the scene logically requires a group of new characters, distribute them as evenly as the scene allows.\\n- If a nonbinary or ungendered role is explicitly required by context, preserve that requirement, but do not use it as an excuse to skew all other new characters toward one side.",
